# E2E verification

If this task changed **user-visible or cross-service** behavior, verify it
before claiming done. Pure-internal changes (types, docs, unit tests, comments)
are exempt.

## Do

1. Look up the touched area in [`e2e/COVERAGE.md`](../../../e2e/COVERAGE.md)
   (workspace) or this repo's Identity **E2E areas** row.
2. If a spec exists, verify the matching tag. When a PR into `dev` is
   open, prefer the preview stack after the `<!-- cartera-preview-stack -->`
   comment is healthy:

   ```bash
   cd e2e
   pnpm test:preview --slug <slug>
   ```

   Prod cheap (`pnpm test:prod:verify --grep @<area>`) cannot validate the
   unmerged branch. Use it when there is no open preview, or after promote.
   For UI review, `pnpm snap <customer|operator|guest> <url>` writes
   `e2e/.snaps/`. `pnpm probe <METHOD> <path>` calls a service as a persona.
3. If no spec exists, **in the same task** add one, or add a
   `required-missing` row in `e2e/COVERAGE.md`. The task is not done otherwise.
4. Treat a red verify as not done — fix the product or the spec, or report the
   failure. Do not skip because "the list is small" or "dev is down".

## Do not

- Write outside scratch names `e2e-run-*`.
- Toggle password-login on the persona accounts (`e2e_customer` /
  `e2e_operator`) — that bricks the suite.

When a cloud agent already opened a PR **into `dev`**, UI and journey checks
prefer the preview alias after the stack comment is healthy:
`pnpm snap` against `https://<slug>-<app>.carteracredit.workers.dev` and
`cd e2e && pnpm test:preview --slug <slug>`. Prod cheap cannot validate the
unmerged branch. Preview stacks skip when the PR has label `no-preview`.
Relink checkout is pinned to the PR branch so the stack matches that commit.
Dev hosts are 404 until `harness/platform/dev-stack-handoff.md` is done.
Local stack: `pnpm --dir harness dev` then `E2E_ENV=local`. `/verify-e2e`
is the runbook.
